# Installed skills
# `npx skills add` copies the canonical skills/ folder into the agents' directories and
# symlinks the rest, so every one of these is a build artifact. skills/ is the source of
# truth and IS committed. `skills-lock.json` is deliberately NOT committed: it is a lock for
# a project that *consumes* skills, and this repository publishes rather than consumes any.
# Committing it here would be circular (source ".") and would invalidate on every edit to
# skills/, making `skills check` report a permanent phantom update against itself.
skills-lock.json
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/
.codex/skills/
.cursor/skills/
.pi/skills/
.continue/skills/
.opencode/skills/
.windsurf/skills/
